      "message": "1) Is there a reason why one is private and the other is not?\n2) I was confused why we need an additional boolean flag, since pending broadcast creations are queued on the `mPendingBroadcastSettings`, so we know that we have a pending broadcast to create if it is not empty. I guess `pending` is ambiguous and we could be more precise here.\n\nIt seems that for `mPendingBroadcastCreate`, \"pending\" means awaiting response, but for `mPendingBroadcastSettings` it means \"yet to be requested and not awaiting the response yet\". This discrepancy confused me a bit. Could we name one with `mAwaitingBroadcastCreateResponse` and the other with `mCreateBroadcastQueue` or something, to distinguish these two different things?",
